## 5. Useful Options

| Command | Option | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `mkdir` | `-p` | Create parent directories |
| `cp` | `-r` | Copy directories recursively |
| `cp` | `-i` | Ask before overwriting |
| `mv` | `-i` | Ask before overwriting |
| `rm` | `-r` | Remove directories recursively |
| `rm` | `-i` | Ask before deleting |

## 6. Interview Questions

**Q1. How do you create an empty file?**

`touch filename`

**Q2. How do you create a directory?**

`mkdir directoryname`

**Q3. What is the difference between cp and mv?**

`cp` copies files, whereas `mv` moves or renames files.

**Q4. What is the difference between rm and rmdir?**

`rm` removes files and can remove directories recursively. `rmdir` removes only empty directories.

**Q5. What is the use of mkdir -p?**

Creates parent directories if they do not exist.

**Q6. How do you copy a directory?**

`cp -r source destination`

**Q7. How do you rename a file?**

`mv oldname newname`

